# Exp44 — Joint Direction × Time Position Transport Stress — FROZEN

Frozen 2026-08-13 after Exp43 result and before any Exp44 joint score.

Question: does the exact original TRAIN-fitted `POSITION_SURV` core transport when direction and chronology are crossed simultaneously, with no refit, interaction, recalibration, threshold or Dwell primary term?

Frozen models:

```text
BASE_SURV
POSITION_SURV
PRIMARY = POSITION_SURV vs BASE_SURV
```

Reuse exact Exp41 cells, `geo0=logit(CorridorPosition)`, `k=1..24`, horizons `15/30/60/120m`.

Joint environments use only already-frozen Exp42 direction and Exp43 time definitions:

```text
VAL_EARLY × FULL_UP
VAL_EARLY × FULL_DOWN
VAL_LATE  × FULL_UP
VAL_LATE  × FULL_DOWN
TEST_EARLY × FULL_UP
TEST_EARLY × FULL_DOWN
TEST_LATE  × FULL_UP
TEST_LATE  × FULL_DOWN
```

Primary within each environment: `STATE_HORIZON_WEIGHTED`; uncertainty = whole-BRT-day bootstrap; coverage >=70%.

Frozen formal gate: `POSITION_SURV vs BASE_SURV` must have Brier and LogLoss CI95 lower bound >0 in all 8 joint environments = 16 mandatory cells.

```text
JOINT_DIRECTION_TIME_POSITION_TRANSPORT=PASS only if all 16 cells pass
ROBUST_POSITION_CORE=PASS only if coverage and 16-cell gate pass
```

Coverage failure => `UNDERPOWERED_JOINT_COVERAGE`, not scientific FAIL.

Diagnostics only: counts, class distributions, horizon gains, EXIT/SIDE AUC, calibration, descriptive direction/time gain differences.

Anti-rescue:

```text
NO alternate time cut or direction definition
NO dropping joint environment
NO horizon subset
NO direction/time interaction
NO direction/era-specific coefficient
NO intercept recalibration
NO Position transform/threshold/bucket
NO Dwell primary rescue
NO Exp38/39 or D1/Clock/Z/Fib/weekday/Scale/Energy/HMM context
NO VAL/TEST refit
NO Exp27 scoring/modification
```

Exp44 failure cannot erase Exp40/41 or separate Exp42/43 Position passes. Historical OOS exploratory; runtime promotion NONE.
